# core/data/talk/grammar/en/surf_a_gesture.tlk - more replies to gestures: hug, shake of the head, nod,
# a gift, walking away (owner: TK; T5b package T5B-SURF1, Surface push A). Content only. The census
# showed these player acts repeat one line per rule most (hug, shake head, nod, give, walk away). Clean
# in any room, no register word, no romance. A hug is a plain hug a resident may decline (a stranger, a
# rival, a child who does not know the player). Rule names start with sa_. Syntax: talkc_gen.py.

# ---- HUG: a plain hug, free to decline ---------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.hug.sa_yes guard: !kid_speaker&!rel=stranger&!rel=rival act: hug
  "Hug received. Filing it under good things, top drawer."
  "Come here. Careful, I'm full of soup and old opinions."
  "A hug! Lovely. Nobody's squeezed me since the last eclipse."
  "Mm, good one. Firm, warm, no elbows. Ten out of ten."
  "Oh, go on then. One hug, and I'll pretend I didn't start it."
  "There we go. That's the stuff. I feel two inches taller."
  "Squeeze accepted. Hold on, my glasses are on crooked now."
  "You hug like someone who means it. Don't ever stop."
  "Right, that was nice. Let me think of a way to be cool about it."
  "Oh, hello, hug! Yes, in, in. Mind the hat."
@rule core.hug.sa_yes_morning guard: time=morning&!kid_speaker&!rel=stranger&!rel=rival act: hug
  "A morning hug! Better than coffee, and much less bitter."
  "Hug before breakfast. That's how the day should start."
@rule core.hug.sa_yes_night guard: time=night&!kid_speaker&!rel=stranger&!rel=rival act: hug
  "A hug at this hour? Perfect. Bedtime hugs count double."
  "Shh, careful. A night hug. The owls are jealous."
@rule core.hug.sa_yes_happy guard: mood=happy&!kid_speaker&!rel=stranger&!rel=rival act: hug
  "[HAPPY]Yes! Hugs! I was feeling cheerful and now I'm stuffed with it."
  "[HAPPY]Ha, bring it in! I'm in a hugging mood already."
@rule core.hug.sa_yes_tired guard: mood=tired&!kid_speaker&!rel=stranger&!rel=rival act: hug
  "Mm, warm. I could fall asleep right here. Don't let me."
  "A hug. Good. I was running low on everything."
@rule core.hug.sa_yes_scared guard: mood=scared&!kid_speaker&!rel=stranger&!rel=rival act: hug
  "[SHOCK]Oh, thank you. Everything's a bit much today, and you're not."
  "Oh, that's helping. A lot. Stay a second."
@rule core.hug.sa_yes_friend guard: rel=friend&!kid_speaker act: hug
  "My favourite hug-giver! The line starts here, and it's just you."
  "Friend hug! Better than the stranger kind. Fewer awkward pats."
@rule core.hug.sa_yes_best guard: rel=best&!kid_speaker act: hug
  "Best-friend hug. The deluxe model. Extra squeeze at the end."
  "There you are! Hugs on arrival, you know the rules."
@rule core.hug.sa_yes_family guard: rel=family&!kid_speaker act: hug
  "Family hug! Mind my ribs. They're older than they look."
  "Aw, come here, you. You always did hug like a bear."
@rule core.hug.sa_yes_acq guard: rel=acquaintance&!kid_speaker act: hug
  "Oh, we're hugging people now. Good, I'm in. Just a short one."
  "A hug from a friendly face. That's the best sort."
@rule core.hug.sa_yes_elder guard: elder&!rel=stranger&!rel=rival act: hug
  "Ooh, I'll take that, dear. These old bones love a squeeze."
  "How sweet. Mind the cardigan, it has a lot of buttons."
@rule core.hug.sa_yes_blunt guard: blunt&!rel=stranger&!rel=rival&!kid_speaker act: hug
  "Fine, short one. Okay, that's enough. Okay, one more."
  "Hug done. Good. Don't tell anyone I liked it."
@rule core.hug.sa_yes_polite guard: polite&!rel=stranger&!rel=rival&!kid_speaker act: hug
  "How thoughtful. Thank you, truly. That was most welcome."
  "Oh, my. What a kind gesture. I accept, warmly."
@rule core.hug.sa_yes_quirky guard: quirky&!rel=stranger&!rel=rival&!kid_speaker act: hug
  "Hug detected. Calibrating, yes, that's squeezing. Excellent."
  "I'll log this as a hug. Subcategory: the good kind."
@rule core.hug.sa_yes_topic guard: topic&!kid_speaker&!rel=stranger&!rel=rival act: hug
  "A hug! Better than talking about {x}. Not by much, but still."
  "Hug first, {x} after. That's my order of business."
  "Okay, hug. And then you can explain why {x} came up."
@rule core.hug.sa_thank guard: !kid_speaker&!rel=stranger&!rel=rival act: thank
  "Thanks, I didn't know I needed that. I'll take another."
  "That was kind. Truly. I'll remember it on a grey day."
  "You're good at that. Thank you. It helped more than I'll say."
  "Cheers for the hug. My day was crumpled and now it's flat again."
  "Thank you. I'd say more but I'm busy feeling better."
@rule core.hug.sa_thank_sad guard: mood=sad&!kid_speaker&!rel=stranger&!rel=rival act: thank
  "[SAD]Thank you. I was dragging a sack of nothing, and you lifted it."
  "[SAD]That helped. Really. Thank you for noticing."
@rule core.hug.sa_joke guard: !kid_speaker&!rel=stranger&!rel=rival act: joke
  "Hug! Quick, someone check my pockets, I'm being charmed."
  "I accept this hug on behalf of my elbows, who were not consulted."
  "Oh good, a hug. I was about to start hugging the wallpaper."
  "Is this a hug or a rescue? Either way, I'm saved."
  "Careful, I'm ticklish in places I haven't found yet."
  "Hugs are free here. Tips are accepted in soup."
  "You've hugged me. That's legally binding. I'll be in touch."
@rule core.hug.sa_laugh guard: !kid_speaker&!rel=stranger&!rel=rival act: laugh
  "Ha! Oh, you got me! That was a sneaky one."
  "Hee, okay, okay, I give up. You win. More hugs."
  "Ha ha, you absolute sweetheart! Do it again."
@rule core.hug.sa_stranger guard: !kid_speaker&rel=stranger act: no
  "Oh, hello! That's friendly, but we've just met. Handshake first?"
  "I'm flattered, truly, but I like a bit of warm-up before a hug."
  "Hm, not yet. Ask me again once I know your favourite soup."
  "Sorry, I'm a slow hugger. Give me a few chats, then yes."
  "Kind of you, but my hugs are reserved. Waving's open to all."
@rule core.hug.sa_stranger_dismiss guard: !kid_speaker&rel=stranger act: dismiss
  "Maybe later. Let's start with names. Mine's on the door."
  "Not just now, thanks. A wave will do nicely."
@rule core.hug.sa_rival guard: !kid_speaker&rel=rival act: no
  "Hug, we're not there yet. Possibly never. Ask again in a decade."
  "No, thank you. I'm still cross about the thing. You know the thing."
  "Not from you, no. I've got a standing order of no hugs. Nothing personal."
@rule core.hug.sa_rival_dismiss guard: !kid_speaker&rel=rival act: dismiss
  "Ha, no. Walk it off, you'll feel better."
  "I'll pass. Go hug a tree. They don't talk back."
@rule core.hug.sa_angry guard: mood=angry&!kid_speaker&!rel=stranger act: no
  "[ANGRY]Not right now. I'm a hot kettle. Give it a minute."
  "[ANGRY]Mm, no. Today I'm all corners. Try again tomorrow."
@rule core.hug.sa_kid_yes guard: kid_speaker&!rel=stranger tags: kid act: hug
  "Hug, hug! Squeeze! I'm a squeezy ball!"
  "[HAPPY]Yay, a hug! You smell like cookies. Do you have cookies?"
  "Okay! Hug, count to five! One, two, five!"
  "I'm hugging you back! Super hard! Wait, not that hard."
  "Hugs are my best thing. I'm the hug champion of the street."
  "A hug! Yes! You can hug the cat too, if she lets you."
@rule core.hug.sa_kid_thank guard: kid_speaker&!rel=stranger tags: kid act: thank
  "Thanks for the hug! It was a good one. Can I have another?"
  "Thank you! That made my tummy feel nice."
  "Thanks! You're cuddly, like a pillow with arms."
@rule core.hug.sa_kid_joke guard: kid_speaker&!rel=stranger tags: kid act: joke
  "You can hug me! But not the dragon. He's shy."
  "Hug me and I turn into a frog! Ribbit! Not really."
  "Hugs cost one cookie. Okay, no, they're free today."
@rule core.hug.sa_kid_laugh guard: kid_speaker&!rel=stranger tags: kid act: laugh
  "Hee hee hee! You hugged me! Do it again, do it again!"
  "Ha ha, too tight! No, just right! Okay, tight again!"
@rule core.hug.sa_kid_no guard: kid_speaker&rel=stranger tags: kid act: no
  "Um, no thank you. I don't hug people I don't know. Can I wave?"
  "I'm too shy for hugs. Can we say hi with our hands instead?"
  "No, thanks. My grown-up says I can pick who I hug. I picked not you."
@rule core.hug.sa_kid_dismiss guard: kid_speaker&rel=stranger tags: kid act: dismiss
  "Nope! But you can see my rock collection. It's super good."
  "Not today. Do you want to see my drawing instead?"
@rule core.hug.sa_kid_rival guard: kid_speaker&rel=rival tags: kid act: no
  "No! You didn't share your crayons. No hugs until crayons."
  "Hm, no. I'm cross with you. Maybe after snack."

# ---- SHAKE_HEAD -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.shake_head.sa_disagree act: disagree
  "Oh, you disagree? Splendid. Argue with me, I'm bored."
  "That's a no from you. I'll note it, and then ignore it."
  "Shaking your head, hm? Your neck's saying something your mouth isn't."
  "Fair enough. Wrong, but fair enough."
  "Okay, no, then. I wasn't married to the idea. Only engaged."
  "You shake your head like that, and I start to doubt myself."
  "I see, we'll take a vote. I'm the only voter. I vote me."
  "A head-shake! The world's smallest protest. I salute you."
@rule core.shake_head.sa_disagree_topic guard: topic act: disagree
  "No to {x}? Bold. Tell me why, and keep it short."
  "You don't agree about {x}? Good. Now we have something to do."
  "Hm, not {x}, then. What would you rather talk about?"
  "A head-shake about {x}. I'll accept that and ask nothing."
@rule core.shake_head.sa_disagree_pro guard: stance=pro act: disagree
  "No? But I like it! I've liked it for years."
  "Hey, I'm a fan of that. You're breaking a fan's heart."
@rule core.shake_head.sa_disagree_con guard: stance=con act: disagree
  "Finally, someone who sees it my way. Shake on it. Your head's still going."
  "Ha, thank goodness. I was hoping we'd agree on that."
@rule core.shake_head.sa_disagree_blunt guard: blunt act: disagree
  "No? Fine. Say what you mean next time, it's cheaper."
  "A shake of the head. Words would be quicker, you know."
@rule core.shake_head.sa_disagree_polite guard: polite act: disagree
  "Oh, dear. I seem to have said the wrong thing. I do apologise."
  "I see you disagree. Please, tell me where I went astray."
@rule core.shake_head.sa_disagree_elder guard: elder act: disagree
  "Well, I never. In my day we said it out loud, dear."
  "No, hm? Young people, always shaking things. Heads, hips, fists."
@rule core.shake_head.sa_repeat act: ask_repeat
  "Wait, that was a no? Or a shake? Or is there a bee?"
  "Hm? Sorry, I missed the answer. Words help me a lot."
  "Was that a no, or are you checking for water in your ears?"
  "I need that in words, please. My head-shake reading is rusty."
  "Hold on, say it again with your mouth. Mine isn't a mind reader."
@rule core.shake_head.sa_repeat_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: ask_repeat
  "Huh, you shook your head? Does that mean no? Or bugs?"
  "Wait, what? Say it with words! I'm learning the words."
@rule core.shake_head.sa_joke act: joke
  "That's a shake with real flair. Judges would give it a nine."
  "A shake of the head! Does it come with a rattle?"
  "Don't shake it too hard. Whatever you've got in there is valuable."
  "No means no, and also, bless you, I thought you sneezed."
  "Careful, you'll shake something loose. Something good, hopefully."
  "I'd shake my head back, but I'd get dizzy. You go ahead."
  "No! My own head says yes. We're in a deadlock."
@rule core.shake_head.sa_complain act: complain
  "Oh, so it's no. No to everything. A big sweeping no."
  "I put a lot of effort into that, and you shake your head."
  "No, hm? I should've brought more snacks to this meeting."
  "Great. Another no. My day's a no collection."
  "That's it? A shake? I wrote a speech."
@rule core.shake_head.sa_complain_tired guard: mood=tired act: complain
  "Ugh, a no. I haven't the energy to argue it. Take it."
  "[SLEEPY]No? Fine. Can we do the arguing after a nap?"
@rule core.shake_head.sa_agree act: agree
  "Right, no, I agree. We're a pair of shaky heads."
  "Exactly. No, never. Not on my watch."
  "Ha, same here. We should start a club. Heads shaken only."
  "My head's shaking too. Look at us, being sensible."
@rule core.shake_head.sa_agree_topic guard: topic act: agree
  "No to {x}, same. It's the only sensible thing to say."
  "Not {x}. Agreed. Some things are best left in the cupboard."
@rule core.shake_head.sa_kid_disagree guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: disagree
  "Nuh-uh! Yes! Okay, I didn't think it through."
  "No? But I wanted it! Why's it a no?"
  "You said no! That's a sad sound. Can I have a yes?"
  "No, okay. Can we do something else? A game?"
@rule core.shake_head.sa_kid_joke guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: joke
  "Shake shake shake! I can do that too! My head's loose!"
  "Don't shake too hard or your brain falls out. I read it somewhere."
@rule core.shake_head.sa_kid_agree guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: agree
  "No, right! No no no, we agree! High five?"
  "Me too! Shake shake! We're the shakiest!"
@rule core.shake_head.sa_kid_complain guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: complain
  "Aww, no? But I asked nicely! Please?"
  "That's not fair! I wanted yes! Yes is better!"

# ---- NOD -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.nod.sa_nod act: nod
  "*nods back* We're a nodding duo. Nobody can stop us now."
  "*gives a solemn nod* Understood. And agreed. And moving on."
  "*nods twice* That's a double. It means extra."
  "*tilts head and nods* Mm. Yes, wise. We've decided."
  "*nods* Good. Excellent. The nod is the most efficient word."
  "*nods slowly, for effect* There. Now it's official."
@rule core.nod.sa_nod_polite guard: polite act: nod
  "*inclines head gracefully* How agreeable. I was hoping you'd say so."
  "*a small bow of the head* Delighted. We see eye to eye."
@rule core.nod.sa_nod_flat guard: flat act: nod
  "*nods, barely* That's me nodding. It took a lot."
  "*one slow nod* Yes. That was it. I'll need a rest now."
@rule core.nod.sa_nod_loud guard: loud act: nod
  "*NODS HARD* YES! WE AGREE! IT'S BEEN SETTLED!"
@rule core.nod.sa_back act: backchannel
  "Mm-hm. Yes, quite. Exactly what I think, as well."
  "Right, you nod, I say mm-hm. That's the rhythm of a good chat."
  "Yeah? Good. I thought you'd see it that way."
  "Mm. Nod noted. I'll carry on, then."
  "Ah, you're with me. Splendid. It's lonely out here."
  "Yes, yes. A nod's worth a thousand words. Or three."
  "Right. Good, we're in step. I do like that."
@rule core.nod.sa_back_topic guard: topic act: backchannel
  "Yes, {x}! You nod like someone who gets it."
  "Exactly. {x:cap}. That's the whole thing, in a nod."
  "A nod for {x}! Good taste. I'm pleased."
@rule core.nod.sa_back_pro guard: stance=pro act: backchannel
  "You like it too? I knew it. We should start a fan club."
  "Yes! A nod from a fellow fan. This is a good day."
@rule core.nod.sa_back_sad guard: mood=sad act: backchannel
  "[SAD]Mm. Thank you for nodding. It helps to be heard."
  "[SAD]Yes. You get it. Not many people do."
@rule core.nod.sa_tell act: tell
  "Oh, right! Nodding, good. Then I'll tell you the rest."
  "I'm glad you nodded, because the next part's a little silly."
  "Well then. Since you're keeping up, here's the thing."
  "Okay, where was I? Ah yes. The bit about the bucket."
  "You're a good listener. Here's the rest, then, and it gets weirder."
  "Good, good. So, as I was saying, the whole cake fell over."
  "Nodding along! You'll love this. Nobody believes the second half."
@rule core.nod.sa_tell_night guard: time=night act: tell
  "Shh, listen. It's a quiet kind of story. Perfect for the dark."
  "Okay, since you're awake: the night shift has some gossip."
@rule core.nod.sa_tell_morning guard: time=morning act: tell
  "Morning chat, and a nod already! Here's what I've got so far."
  "Good. Okay. Before breakfast I'd like to tell you something."
@rule core.nod.sa_joke act: joke
  "You nod like a woodpecker. It's a good look. Bit loud."
  "A nod! Or was that a sleepy lurch? I'll take it either way."
  "Keep nodding, and we'll agree on everything. That's my plan."
  "A nod is a yes with the sound off. I respect it."
  "Your head went up and down. Mine's going to do the same. Watch."
  "Careful, if you nod enough I'll start making promises."
@rule core.nod.sa_cont act: continue
  "Okay, I'll go on. You nodded, so I take it as a licence."
  "Right, more of it, then. Don't say I didn't warn you."
  "Good. Next bit. It's about a hat, and I'm sorry."
  "Since you're still here, I'll carry on. Strap in."
  "More? You nodded, so here's more. Go slowly, it's fragile."
@rule core.nod.sa_cont_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: continue
  "Okay, and then! And then, wait, I forgot. Okay, and then!"
  "You nodded, so I'll keep going! There's a giant in it!"
@rule core.nod.sa_kid_nod guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: nod
  "*nods like a bobblehead* Yes yes yes yes! Look, I'm fast!"
  "*nods super duper hard* Nod nod nod! We're best nodders!"
  "*nods and nods* My head's going to fall off! It's fine!"
@rule core.nod.sa_kid_tell guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: tell
  "You nodded! That means I can tell you my secret! It's a snail."
  "Okay, so, today I saw a bird. It was big. That's all."
@rule core.nod.sa_kid_back guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: backchannel
  "Yeah! You get it! You get everything!"
  "Mm-hm! I knew you'd say yes! Grown-ups know stuff!"

# ---- GIVE: a gift -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.give.sa_thank act: thank
  "Oh, thank you! It's so thoughtful. Nobody gets me things."
  "For me, I'm speechless. Give me a moment. Okay, still speechless."
  "Thank you! I'll put it somewhere I can see it. And fuss."
  "You didn't have to. I'm glad you did, though. I'm very glad."
  "Aw, it's perfect. How did you know? Have you been watching me?"
  "I accept! With gratitude, and with both hands, and a sniff."
  "A gift! I'll be unbearable about it for a week."
  "Thanks, that's the nicest thing today. And it's still morning."
@rule core.give.sa_thank_sad guard: mood=sad act: thank
  "[SAD]Oh. Thank you. I needed something nice today."
  "[SAD]That's very kind. You've made a grey day a bit brighter."
@rule core.give.sa_thank_friend guard: rel=friend act: thank
  "From you? I'll treasure it. Friends give the best presents."
  "Oh, you, thank you. You always know. It's a talent."
@rule core.give.sa_thank_best guard: rel=best act: thank
  "Best friend, best present. I'll put it on the shelf of honour."
  "You spoil me. Thank you. I'll find a way to pay you back in soup."
@rule core.give.sa_thank_stranger guard: rel=stranger act: thank
  "Oh! We've only just met, and you're giving me things. How nice."
  "That's generous, for a stranger. Thank you. I'll make it count."
@rule core.give.sa_thank_family guard: rel=family act: thank
  "Aw, family always knows. Thank you, I'll keep it close."
@rule core.give.sa_thank_topic guard: topic act: thank
  "Thank you. It goes with {x}, which is a nice touch."
  "A gift, it reminds me of {x}. Somehow. Thank you."
@rule core.give.sa_thank_elder guard: elder act: thank
  "Bless you, dear. It's been a while since someone brought me a present."
  "How thoughtful! I'll show it to the girls at tea."
@rule core.give.sa_thank_blunt guard: blunt act: thank
  "Hm, good. Thanks. I'll use it, which is high praise."
  "Fine, thanks. It's decent. Don't look so smug."
@rule core.give.sa_thank_flat guard: flat act: thank
  "Thanks, I'm delighted. This is my delighted face. Look closely."
@rule core.give.sa_joke act: joke
  "Is it a bribe? Because it works. What do you want?"
  "A present! Is it alive? Please say it isn't alive."
  "Gifts! My favourite kind of unprompted event."
  "You've gifted me! Now I'm obliged to like you. Clever."
  "I'll give you a hug, but I want the box too. The box is the best bit."
  "Is it ticking? It's not ticking. Good, thank you."
  "Careful, if you keep giving me things, I'll move in."
@rule core.give.sa_pos act: opine_pos
  "This is wonderful. I'll cherish it. And I'll show it to people."
  "Oh, it's lovely. It's the right size, too, which is rare."
  "It's just what I needed. I mean it. I'd forgotten I needed it."
  "How clever! You've got a good eye. I'll use it all the time."
  "A very nice thing, this. I like the weight of it."
@rule core.give.sa_pos_topic guard: topic act: opine_pos
  "I'd never have thought of {x}, but this is perfect for it."
  "Ooh, now I want to talk about {x} all afternoon."
@rule core.give.sa_pos_pro guard: stance=pro act: opine_pos
  "You remembered what I like! That's the best part."
  "It's perfect. You've got me figured out. Rude, but lovely."
@rule core.give.sa_neg act: opine_neg
  "It's, um, a gift. A gift's a gift. I'll find a spot."
  "Oh, it's interesting. I'll put it somewhere safe. Out of sight."
  "Hm, well. The thought counts. And I'm thinking hard."
  "I'm not sure what it does. But I'll keep it. Out of politeness."
  "It's... unusual. In the sense that I've never seen one."
@rule core.give.sa_neg_con guard: stance=con act: opine_neg
  "Oh, dear, you've picked the one thing I can't stand. Thank you, anyway."
  "Ha, I do not like this, but I like you. Kind of you."
@rule core.give.sa_kid_thank guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: thank
  "Wow, a present! Is it for keeps? Thank you thank you!"
  "Thank you! I'll hide it in my secret place. Don't tell!"
  "For me, really? Can I open it now? I'm opening it."
  "Yay! I love presents! I'll give you my second-best stick."
@rule core.give.sa_kid_joke guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: joke
  "Is it a frog? I hope it's a frog. A nice frog."
  "A present, is it candy? Is it a pony? It's a sock, right?"
@rule core.give.sa_kid_pos guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: opine_pos
  "I love it! It's the best! I'll sleep with it tonight!"
  "It's awesome! It's shiny! You're the best at presents!"
@rule core.give.sa_kid_neg guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: opine_neg
  "Um, thanks? What does it do? Does it do anything?"
  "Hm, it's weird. But weird is good. I think."

# ---- WALK_AWAY: the player leaves mid-chat --------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.walk_away.sa_bye act: farewell
  "Oh, bye! Off already? Well, don't let the door hit your shadow."
  "Going? Okay, I'll keep the seat warm. Or cold, I'll try."
  "Leaving mid-sentence is a bold move. Respect. Bye."
  "Fine, fine, off you pop. Mind the third step, it bites."
  "Bye then! I'll tell the next person your half of the story."
  "See you around. I'll be here, standing in my own sentences."
  "Running along? Right, don't fall in anything. Bye."
  "Leaving, that's okay. I'll talk to the plant. It listens."
@rule core.walk_away.sa_bye_night guard: time=night act: farewell
  "Off into the dark? Careful out there. Take a lamp."
  "Goodnight, then. Mind the moon, it's tricky tonight."
@rule core.walk_away.sa_bye_morning guard: time=morning act: farewell
  "Off so early? Well, good luck. Bring me a story later."
  "Morning dash, huh? Don't forget breakfast. Breakfast is important."
@rule core.walk_away.sa_bye_friend guard: rel=friend act: farewell
  "Going already? Okay. Drop by again soon, I'll hold the chair."
  "Aw, you're off. Don't be a stranger, we only have a few."
@rule core.walk_away.sa_bye_best guard: rel=best act: farewell
  "Bye, you. Text me if the sky falls. Or if it's just clouds."
  "Off you go. I'll pretend I'm not sad. I'm sad, hurry back."
@rule core.walk_away.sa_bye_family guard: rel=family act: farewell
  "Leaving already? Take a coat, and a snack. And a bit of me."
  "Go on, then. Call when you get there. I'll worry quietly."
@rule core.walk_away.sa_bye_polite guard: polite act: farewell
  "Oh, farewell, then. It was a pleasure. Do come again."
  "Goodbye! Thank you for the company. Mind how you go."
@rule core.walk_away.sa_bye_blunt guard: blunt act: farewell
  "Bye, don't slam the door. Or do. See if I care."
  "Leaving, then? Good, I need quiet. See you."
@rule core.walk_away.sa_bye_elder guard: elder act: farewell
  "Off you go, dear. These legs can't keep up anymore."
  "Goodbye, then. Wrap up warm, the fog gets in the bones."
@rule core.walk_away.sa_bye_topic guard: topic act: farewell
  "Off already? We hadn't finished with {x}. Another time, then."
  "Bye! Leave {x} with me, I'll look after it."
@rule core.walk_away.sa_complain act: complain
  "Hey! I wasn't finished! I was building to something."
  "Oh, charming. Walk away, why don't you. I'll just stand here."
  "There they go. Mid-story. I've been abandoned by my own audience."
  "Wow. That's how it is. I'll tell the wall instead."
  "Typical. I finally get a good punchline and nobody's there."
  "Fine, fine, go. See if I save you any biscuits."
@rule core.walk_away.sa_complain_sad guard: mood=sad act: complain
  "[SAD]Oh. You're going. I was hoping you'd stay a bit."
  "[SAD]Right, people leave. That's okay. I'm fine, really."
@rule core.walk_away.sa_complain_angry guard: mood=angry act: complain
  "[ANGRY]Fine! Walk away, just like that! See if I mind!"
  "[ANGRY]Oh, now you leave. I've got more to say, too."
@rule core.walk_away.sa_joke act: joke
  "And so the hero left the chat, never to be seen again. Until lunch."
  "Mysterious stranger walks out. Cue a dramatic gust of wind."
  "That was the shortest talk I've had. A record. I'll frame it."
  "Wait, come back! I have gossip! Okay, I'll yell it at your back."
  "The player has left the building. Please enjoy this silence."
  "Goodbye! I've been told my chat's a hit-and-run. Here we are."
  "Off so soon? And I'd practised my entire speech. Twice."
@rule core.walk_away.sa_dismiss act: dismiss
  "Right, go, then. I've got things to do. Important things."
  "Whatever. Leaving's fine. I wasn't enjoying it anyway."
  "Okay, off with you. Don't let me keep you from nothing."
  "Sure. Go. I'll be over here, being fine."
@rule core.walk_away.sa_dismiss_blunt guard: blunt act: dismiss
  "Good. I've got a nap planned and you're in the way."
  "Off you go. Try the exit. It's the big flat thing."
@rule core.walk_away.sa_kid_bye guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: farewell
  "Bye bye, see you tomorrow! Or next week! Or now!"
  "You're going? Okay. Wave at me from the corner!"
  "Bye! Come back and see my drawing! It's got a dog!"
@rule core.walk_away.sa_kid_complain guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: complain
  "Wait, don't go! I wasn't done! I had a big thing!"
  "Hey! You can't just walk! We were having fun!"
  "Aw, no, come back! I'll share my snack! Half of it!"
@rule core.walk_away.sa_kid_joke guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: joke
  "Walk walk walk! You're a walking robot! Beep beep!"
  "Bye, mind the lava! It's the pavement! Actually it's the grass!"
@rule core.walk_away.sa_kid_dismiss guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: dismiss
  "Okay. Go, I've got toys. They don't leave."
  "Fine, fine. I'm busy anyway. I'm very busy playing."
